 "method": "Headless Chromium against the anonymous canonical hub with real published, registered children. Menu card opened by tap (touch sizes) or keyboard Enter (desktop, reduced motion). Ordinary clicks/taps only; no route interception, fake parent, DOM removal, badge removal or relaxed security flags. Parent and child sampled about every 0.3 s; 'child loader visible' means the child's own progress percentage was rendered with effective opacity above 0.5. Ready = real ready postMessage observed by the parent page.",
 "summary": {
  "launches": 24,
  "hubStartingCoverOverChildLoader": 0,
  "openingTextWhileChildPresent": 0,
  "trains": "Child loader visible 9.8-22.9 s cold/cached in all 12 launches; no hub slow cover; ready 5.7-14.5 s (slower when six runs shared the network). 6/6 Next presses hit the real Next button unobstructed and promoted the same prepared iframe and seed; Back returned to ?band=4.",
  "money-change": "Child loader visible 33-49 s in all 12 launches; real story intro with Begin after ready. In all 12 launches (and all 6 post-Next promotions) the hub's 20-second slow cover appeared at about 20 s and covered the child loader until real ready at 33-47 s, then cleared by itself. 6/6 Next presses (after Begin) promoted the same prepared iframe and seed; Back returned to ?band=4."
 },
 "limitations": [
  "Till: the hub's existing 20-second slow cover ('This adventure is taking a while to open.' / Try again / All games) obscures Till's own loader and its 'Start with the market picture' fallback button for roughly 13-27 s on every launch, because Till's real ready arrives after 33-47 s. Not a false failure: it clears on real ready. Not changed, per scope (no timeout/readiness changes). Fix options need approval: Till sends ready earlier from its own fallback path, or a per-game hub timeout.",
  "All games: the hub shows its 'Opening your adventure' cover for up to ~0.5 s right after the card tap, before any game iframe exists (while the session rechecks availability). It never drew over a child document.",
  "Till after Next: the prepared Till instance was usually not ready yet, so its loader (and later the 20 s slow cover) appeared again after promotion.",
  "Train Lovable badge: no badge element was found in the embedded Train document; at 393x852 Next sat at x291 y802 76x44, the hit test landed on the button and the ordinary tap worked in all six sizes. The standalone Train page outside the hub was not checked.",
  "Till shows a zero-size Lovable badge element (id lovable-badge-cta) inside its document; it did not intercept any tested control.",
  "No Till or Train puzzle was solved; Next was pressed with the games' own Next buttons.",
  "Public child sourceVersion values differ from the user-stated published SHAs; build IDs match the registry entries.",
  "Headless Chromium only; no physical iPad or Safari testing."
 ],
